# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto
package.json text eol=lf
.husky/pre-push text eol=lf

# --- NASA SVS 5073 eclipse fixture (C12-29 S5) ---------------------------------
# Every member of this directory is pinned by SHA-256 in the fixture manifest and
# in the queue stamps, so a checkout that rewrites even one byte invalidates the
# provenance chain rather than producing a diff someone would notice.
#
# Correction 2026-08-14 (fix SOL-12; audit finding S21 of
# SOL_WEEK_AUDIT_2026-08-14.md, corroborated independently by three lanes): before
# this block the three binary members were covered only by git's own binary
# heuristic and the `.prj` was left under `* text=auto`. With `core.autocrlf=true`
# on Windows -- this repository's normal configuration -- that made the byte-identity
# claim true only by accident: the `.prj` happens to contain NO CR and NO LF byte
# (verified: 143 bytes, 0x0D x0, 0x0A x0), so normalization had nothing to rewrite.
# The other three DO carry EOL bytes inside binary records (.dbf 1 CR / 2 LF,
# .shp 15 CR / 10 LF, .shx 0 CR / 1 LF) and would be silently corrupted if the
# heuristic ever guessed "text". Declare every member explicitly instead of relying
# on either accident.
#
# `-text` disables all EOL conversion in both directions; `binary` is the shorthand
# for `-text -diff` and additionally stops git from attempting a textual diff.
Tools/visual-regression/fixtures/nasa-svs-5073/*.shp binary
Tools/visual-regression/fixtures/nasa-svs-5073/*.shx binary
Tools/visual-regression/fixtures/nasa-svs-5073/*.dbf binary
# The projection file is human-readable WKT but is hashed byte-for-byte alongside
# the binaries, so it is pinned with `-text` rather than `eol=lf`: `-text` cannot be
# defeated by a future editor writing CRLF into the working tree, whereas `eol=lf`
# only normalizes on the way in.
Tools/visual-regression/fixtures/nasa-svs-5073/*.prj -text
# Tooling and metadata are ordinary text and are normalized to LF so they are
# stable across platforms.
Tools/visual-regression/fixtures/nasa-svs-5073/manifest.json text eol=lf
Tools/visual-regression/fixtures/nasa-svs-5073/NOTICE.md text eol=lf
Tools/visual-regression/fixtures/nasa-svs-5073/*.mjs text eol=lf
migration_doc/pending/*.diff -text

# --- Shared probe runtime -------------------------------------------------------
# Same mechanism as the fixture block above, different consequence. `* text=auto`
# plus `core.autocrlf=true` means an ordinary text file is stored LF and checked
# out CRLF, and two things in this set cannot survive that:
#   * the banked pre-runtime receipt is compared byte-for-byte against the
#     runtime's own `normalizeJson` output, which is LF by definition -- a CRLF
#     checkout fails the provenance sentinel that keeps the fixture from being
#     regenerated out of the file under test;
#   * the spec's inertness mutants anchor on literal source text spanning a
#     newline, so a CRLF checkout matches the anchor zero times and trips the
#     occurs-exactly-once guard.
# Verified: an out-of-tree copy of these files rewritten to CRLF goes 47/47 ->
# 43/47 on `node --test probe-runtime.spec.mjs`. The spec was ALSO made
# EOL-tolerant (it normalizes what it reads), so this block is the fix and that
# is its belt -- neither alone should be relied on.
Tools/visual-regression/fixtures/probe-runtime/*.json text eol=lf
Tools/visual-regression/lib/probe-runtime.mjs text eol=lf
Tools/visual-regression/lib/probe-edge-slot.mjs text eol=lf
Tools/visual-regression/lib/probe-refusal.mjs text eol=lf
Tools/visual-regression/probe-runtime.spec.mjs text eol=lf
Tools/visual-regression/probe-globe-cold-start-readiness.mjs text eol=lf
